<mjml><mj-head><mj-title>GatorBait Magazine: Friday Pregame, Florida at Missouri</mj-title><mj-preview>Franz Beard leads the Friday pregame edition: the Sooth Board, three keys and who is out.</mj-preview><mj-attributes><mj-all font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" /><mj-text color="#11274A" font-size="16px" line-height="1.5" /><mj-button background-color="#FA4616" color="#FFFFFF" border-radius="3px" font-size="15px" font-weight="800" /></mj-attributes></mj-head><mj-body background-color="#EEF1F5">
<mj-section background-color="#FA4616" padding="8px 16px"><mj-column><mj-text align="center" color="#FFFFFF" font-size="13px" font-weight="800" padding="0">TEST EMAIL for Brenden only. Not sent to the list.</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="18px 24px 14px" border-bottom="4px solid #FA4616"><mj-column><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_95dd8a25863b4556b7ba6398fcfd0316~mv2.webp/v1/fit/w_600,h_160,q_90/file.png" alt="GatorBait" width="250px" href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/magazine" padding="0" /><mj-text align="center" color="#081F3D" font-size="12px" font-weight="800" letter-spacing="2.4px" padding="8px 0 0">MAGAZINE &#183; FRIDAY PREGAME EDITION &#183; OCT. 2, 2026</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#081F3D" padding="0"><mj-column><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_12f2b9b8ad7b4a7b99b66dabc7e694ea~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1200,h_1600,al_c,q_85/file.jpg" alt="GatorBait Magazine cover: Gators head to Missouri, where history hasn’t been kind. Photo by Chris Spears, GatorBait Media." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/the-soothsayer-gators-head-to-missouri-where-history-hasn-t-been-kind" padding="0" width="600px" /></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="22px 24px 6px"><mj-column><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="17px" line-height="1.5" padding="0 0 6px">No. 8 Florida (4-0) is 2-4 in Columbia since 2012 and has to find an emotional peak right after the biggest win in years. Franz Beard asks if the Gators are tough enough.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/the-soothsayer-gators-head-to-missouri-where-history-hasn-t-been-kind" padding="14px 0 6px">READ THE COLUMN</mj-button><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/magazine" background-color="#081F3D" padding="6px 0 10px">OPEN THE FULL MAGAZINE</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#081F3D" padding="26px 24px 8px"><mj-column><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0 0 8px">THE GAME &#183; SATURDAY, OCT. 3 · 3:30 P.M. ET &#183; ABC</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="32px" line-height="1.08" font-weight="900" padding="0 0 8px">No. 8 Florida at No. 25 Missouri</mj-text><mj-text color="#D7E0EB" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="0">Memorial Stadium (Faurot Field), Columbia, Mo. &#183; 71°, 0% chance of rain, gusts to 10 mph (ESPN forecast, Oct. 1)<br/>Line Florida -5.5 &#183; Total 57.5 &#183; Moneyline FLA -218 · MIZ +180<br/>ESPN data as of Oct. 1-2, 2026. Kickoff, line and forecast can move before Saturday.<br/>ESPN matchup predictor: Florida 70.2%, Missouri 29.8%.</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="26px 24px 6px"><mj-column><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0 0 6px">THE SOOTHSAYER</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="30px" line-height="1.1" font-weight="900" padding="0 0 4px">The Sooth Board</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="14px" padding="0 0 8px">Saturday&#8217;s SEC games with Franz Beard&#8217;s picks. Kickoffs, TV and lines: ESPN.</mj-text><mj-table padding="0" cellpadding="0"><tr><td style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;"><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;color:#0A2CA8;letter-spacing:1.2px;">NOON &#183; ABC</div><div style="font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;line-height:1.25;padding:2px 0;">No. 7 Alabama (4-0) at No. 16 Mississippi State (4-0)</div><div style="font-size:13px;color:#4B586A;">Line ALA -6 &#183; O/U 60.5</div><div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;padding-top:3px;">Franz&#8217;s pick: Alabama</div></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;"><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;color:#0A2CA8;letter-spacing:1.2px;">12:45 P.M. &#183; SEC NETWORK</div><div style="font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;line-height:1.25;padding:2px 0;">Vanderbilt (3-1) at No. 2 Georgia (4-0)</div><div style="font-size:13px;color:#4B586A;">Line UGA -25.5 &#183; O/U 50.5</div><div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;padding-top:3px;">Franz&#8217;s pick: Georgia</div></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;background:#FFF4EF;"><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;color:#0A2CA8;letter-spacing:1.2px;">3:30 P.M. &#183; ABC</div><div style="font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;line-height:1.25;padding:2px 0;">No. 8 Florida (4-0) at No. 25 Missouri (3-1)</div><div style="font-size:13px;color:#4B586A;">Line FLA -5.5 &#183; O/U 57.5</div><div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;padding-top:3px;">Franz&#8217;s pick: Florida by more than 5.5</div></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;"><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;color:#0A2CA8;letter-spacing:1.2px;">3:30 P.M. &#183; ESPN</div><div style="font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;line-height:1.25;padding:2px 0;">Auburn (3-1) at No. 17 Tennessee (3-1)</div><div style="font-size:13px;color:#4B586A;">Line TENN -7 &#183; O/U 53.5</div><div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;padding-top:3px;">Franz&#8217;s pick: Tennessee</div></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;"><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;color:#0A2CA8;letter-spacing:1.2px;">4:15 P.M. &#183; SEC NETWORK</div><div style="font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;line-height:1.25;padding:2px 0;">No. 24 Kentucky (3-1) at South Carolina (2-2)</div><div style="font-size:13px;color:#4B586A;">Line SC -3 &#183; O/U 54.5</div><div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;padding-top:3px;">Franz&#8217;s pick: Kentucky</div></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;"><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;color:#0A2CA8;letter-spacing:1.2px;">7 P.M. &#183; ESPN2</div><div style="font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;line-height:1.25;padding:2px 0;">Arkansas (2-2) at Texas A&amp;M (2-2)</div><div style="font-size:13px;color:#4B586A;">Line TA&amp;M -13.5 &#183; O/U 50.5</div><div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;padding-top:3px;">Franz&#8217;s pick: Texas A&amp;M</div></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3ec;"><div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:800;color:#0A2CA8;letter-spacing:1.2px;">7:45 P.M. &#183; SEC NETWORK</div><div style="font-size:18px;font-weight:900;color:#081F3D;line-height:1.25;padding:2px 0;">McNeese (2-3) at No. 11 LSU (3-1)</div><div style="font-size:13px;color:#4B586A;">Line LSU -53.5 &#183; O/U 62.5</div><div style="font-size:15px;font-weight:900;color:#FA4616;padding-top:3px;">Franz&#8217;s pick: LSU</div></td></tr></mj-table></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="18px 24px 6px"><mj-column><mj-divider border-color="#dde3ec" border-width="1px" padding="0 0 12px" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0">THREE KEYS</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="20px" line-height="1.2" font-weight="900" padding="12px 0 2px">1. Baugh against a top-20 run defense</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="0 0 4px">Florida runs for 260 yards a game and has 18 rushing touchdowns, tied for most in the country.</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="20px" line-height="1.2" font-weight="900" padding="12px 0 2px">2. Philo’s shots against a bend-don’t-break secondary</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="0 0 4px">Aaron Philo’s 10.5 yards an attempt leads the SEC and he has been sacked twice in 104 throws.</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="20px" line-height="1.2" font-weight="900" padding="12px 0 2px">3. Third downs and Austin Simmons</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="0 0 4px">Florida allows 248 passing yards a game, 113th nationally, and opponents convert 41% on third down.</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="14px 24px 22px"><mj-column><mj-divider border-color="#dde3ec" border-width="1px" padding="0 0 12px" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0">WHO IS OUT</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="13px" padding="2px 0 0">As of Oct. 1. ESPN lists no injuries for either team; names below are GatorBait reporting.</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="17px" font-weight="900" padding="10px 0 2px">Florida</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="14px" line-height="1.6" padding="0 0 4px">WR Vernell Brown III &#8212; <b>Questionable</b><br/>WR Bailey Stockton &#8212; <b>Questionable</b></mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="17px" font-weight="900" padding="10px 0 2px">Missouri</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="14px" line-height="1.6" padding="0 0 4px">S JaDon Blair &#8212; <b>Out</b><br/>RB Ahmad Hardy &#8212; <b>Out</b><br/>RB Malae Fonoti &#8212; <b>Out</b><br/>OL Josh Atkins &#8212; <b>Out</b><br/>TE Gavin Hoffman &#8212; <b>Out</b><br/>EDGE Langden Kitchen &#8212; <b>Questionable</b><br/>EDGE Darris Smith &#8212; <b>Questionable</b></mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#081F3D" padding="26px 24px 4px"><mj-column><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0 0 4px">THIS WEEK</mj-text><mj-text color="#FFFFFF" font-size="28px" font-weight="900" padding="0">More from GatorBait</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="0 0 2px"><mj-column><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_408fa442a2d54309aa66050fb0f4d35e~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1200,h_674,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="Jon Sumrall reacts on the Florida sideline with an official in the foreground (Photo by Chris Spears, GatorBait Media)" href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/coaches-and-fans-have-different-playbooks-so-have-another-round-thirsty-gators" padding="0" width="600px" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="14px 24px 0">BUDDY MARTIN · COLUMN</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="22px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="4px 24px 0">Coaches and Fans Have Different Playbooks. So Have Another Round, Thirsty Gators.</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="6px 24px 0">Florida fans have earned the right to brag after four years of misery. Just don’t build a shrine on an early poll before Saturday’s trip to Missouri.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/coaches-and-fans-have-different-playbooks-so-have-another-round-thirsty-gators" align="left" padding="10px 24px 22px" inner-padding="10px 22px">READ</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="0 0 2px"><mj-column><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_56a64986c874417c9a8299fae22649ed~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1200,h_674,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="Buddy Martin column: The Looming Brilliance of Buster Faulkner. Photo by Chris Spears, GatorBait Media; Faulkner photo UAA." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/the-looming-brilliance-of-buster-faulkner-if-it-works-one-time-we-retire-it" padding="0" width="600px" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="14px 24px 0">BUDDY MARTIN · COLUMN</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="22px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="4px 24px 0">The Looming Brilliance of Buster Faulkner: “If It Works Once, We Retire It”</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="6px 24px 0">This guy could turn out to be brilliant. Maybe even Steve Spurrier brilliant. But Faulkner has to earn that.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/the-looming-brilliance-of-buster-faulkner-if-it-works-one-time-we-retire-it" align="left" padding="10px 24px 22px" inner-padding="10px 22px">READ</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="0 0 2px"><mj-column><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_f130d47a9cb74914b869ac554c67e931~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1200,h_674,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="Officials at the SEC replay monitor on the Florida sideline (Photo by Chris Spears, GatorBait Media)" href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/florida-keeps-winning-big-and-the-laundry-keeps-piling-up" padding="0" width="600px" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="14px 24px 0">ANALYSIS · GATORBAIT STAFF</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="22px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="4px 24px 0">Florida Keeps Winning Big, and the Laundry Keeps Piling Up</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="6px 24px 0">The No. 8 Gators have outscored four opponents by nearly 31 points a game while drawing 35 flags for 357 yards.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/florida-keeps-winning-big-and-the-laundry-keeps-piling-up" align="left" padding="10px 24px 22px" inner-padding="10px 22px">READ</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="0 0 2px"><mj-column><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/16b519_00359caad82744778e7c387d8bf98777~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1200,h_674,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="Aaron Philo, Florida quarterback (Photo by Chris Spears, GatorBait Media)" href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/when-it-came-to-finding-a-quarterback-sumrall-trusted-buster-and-it-paid-off" padding="0" width="600px" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="14px 24px 0">FRANZ BEARD · COLUMN</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="22px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="4px 24px 0">When it came to finding a quarterback Sumrall trusted Buster and it paid off</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="6px 24px 0">Aaron Philo was barely known when the season began. Jon Sumrall trusted Buster Faulkner to find a quarterback, and it paid off.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/when-it-came-to-finding-a-quarterback-sumrall-trusted-buster-and-it-paid-off" align="left" padding="10px 24px 22px" inner-padding="10px 22px">READ</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="0 0 2px"><mj-column><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_dc70ea9e65574abebd3b0ace40bd8232~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1200,h_674,al_c,q_80/file.png" alt="Jayden Woods, Florida JACK linebacker (Graphic: GatorBait Media)" href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/jayden-woods-added-to-chuck-bednarik-award-watch-list" padding="0" width="600px" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="14px 24px 0">HONORS · GATORBAIT STAFF</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="22px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="4px 24px 0">Jayden Woods Added To Chuck Bednarik Award Watch List</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="6px 24px 0">The sophomore JACK’s 19 tackles, six TFLs and four sacks through four games have him in the running for college football’s top defensive honor.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/jayden-woods-added-to-chuck-bednarik-award-watch-list" align="left" padding="10px 24px 22px" inner-padding="10px 22px">READ</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="0 0 2px"><mj-column><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_a67ff355ad6a4d668106c2befa41b208~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1200,h_674,al_c,q_80/file.png" alt="Show-Me State of Mind: No. 8 Florida at No. 25 Missouri, Saturday, Oct. 3, 3:30 p.m. ET. GatorBait Media graphic." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/first-look-missouri-florida-gators-show-me-state-of-mind" padding="0" width="600px" /><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="1.6px" padding="14px 24px 0">PREVIEW · GATORBAIT STAFF</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="22px" line-height="1.15" font-weight="900" padding="4px 24px 0">Show-Me State of Mind: A First Look at No. 25 Missouri</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="15px" line-height="1.5" padding="6px 24px 0">No. 8 Florida’s reward for routing Ole Miss is a trip to No. 25 Missouri, which let a fourth-quarter lead get away at Mississippi State.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/first-look-missouri-florida-gators-show-me-state-of-mind" align="left" padding="10px 24px 22px" inner-padding="10px 22px">READ</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="22px 21px 0"><mj-column><mj-text color="#FA4616" font-size="12px" font-weight="900" letter-spacing="2px" padding="0 3px 2px">PHOTOGRAPHY</mj-text><mj-text color="#081F3D" font-size="26px" font-weight="900" padding="0 3px 4px">Best shots</mj-text><mj-text color="#4B586A" font-size="13px" padding="0 3px 4px">From Florida 52, Ole Miss 28. Photos by Chris Spears, GatorBait Media.</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="0 21px"><mj-column padding="3px"><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/16b519_9e6aad749e564c33ab69f6e7e19e9560~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_360,h_240,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="The Swamp before kickoff against Ole Miss." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/chris-spears-best-shots-vol-2-florida-52-ole-miss-28" padding="0" /><mj-text font-size="12px" color="#4B586A" padding="3px 0 0" line-height="1.3">The Swamp before kickoff</mj-text></mj-column><mj-column padding="3px"><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/16b519_958769d0cfef4d9e931621ae78bfd008~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_360,h_240,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="Gators players celebrate a touchdown against Ole Miss." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/chris-spears-best-shots-vol-2-florida-52-ole-miss-28" padding="0" /><mj-text font-size="12px" color="#4B586A" padding="3px 0 0" line-height="1.3">Celebrating a touchdown</mj-text></mj-column><mj-column padding="3px"><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/16b519_ab5daac7afa94664b9e6a4931049cfb9~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_360,h_240,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="Florida defenders make a tackle against Ole Miss." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/chris-spears-best-shots-vol-2-florida-52-ole-miss-28" padding="0" /><mj-text font-size="12px" color="#4B586A" padding="3px 0 0" line-height="1.3">The defense swarms</mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="0 21px 8px"><mj-column padding="3px"><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d3cfa5_ce8defc3525b4e74a6a394170740c270~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_360,h_240,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="Jon Sumrall leads the Gators onto the field." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/chris-spears-best-shots-vol-2-florida-52-ole-miss-28" padding="0" /><mj-text font-size="12px" color="#4B586A" padding="3px 0 0" line-height="1.3">Sumrall leads the Gators out</mj-text></mj-column><mj-column padding="3px"><mj-image src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/16b519_f3af81d3cac048ae84d89d9194ddd9eb~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_360,h_240,al_c,q_80/file.jpg" alt="A Florida player speaks with reporters after the win." href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/post/chris-spears-best-shots-vol-2-florida-52-ole-miss-28" padding="0" /><mj-text font-size="12px" color="#4B586A" padding="3px 0 0" line-height="1.3">After the win</mj-text></mj-column><mj-column padding="3px"></mj-column></mj-section>
<mj-section background-color="#FFFFFF" padding="6px 24px 26px"><mj-column><mj-text align="center" color="#11274A" font-size="16px" padding="0 0 6px">Next up: South Carolina, Oct. 10, in The Swamp. Then Texas in Austin on Oct. 17.</mj-text><mj-button href="https://www.gatorbaitmedia.com/magazine" padding="8px 0 0">OPEN THE FULL MAGAZINE</mj-button></mj-column></mj-section>
